<br><br><aside>							
							
			
				<section id="rd-steps"><h2 id="ref-steps" class="title">Preparation</h2><div class="rd-times"><div class="rdt-item"><i>Preparation</i>15 min</div><div class="rdt-item"><i>Waiting time</i>2 min</div><div class="rdt-item"><i>Cook time</i>30 min</div></div><ul class="rd-steps"><li>Separate the egg whites from the yolks. Whisk the yolks with sugar until the mixture is foamy.</li><li>Add skyr and cornstarch, then mix well. Add the chocolate chips and combine.</li><li>Whisk the egg whites until stiff peaks form, then gently fold them into the mixture using a spatula, being careful not to deflate them.</li><li>Pour the batter into a bundt pan and bake for 30 minutes at 350°F (180°C). 			<div id="div-gpt-ad-PC_mobile_336x280_1-0" style="min-width:336px;min-height:300px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align:center; "></div></li><li>Allow the cake to cool before unmolding it onto a plate. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour. Ideally, make this cake the night before (or in the morning for the evening) to ensure an extra fresh tasting experience! Enjoy!</li></ul></section><section id="vote-comments-just-from" class="vote-comments" data-table-name="feed_data" data-table-id="1576186" data-table-member-id="510842" data-table-member-username="PetitChef_Official" data-table-member-photo="/imgupl/member/xs-510842.jpg" data-comment-photo-enabled="1" aria-label="Rating / Comments"><h2 class="title" data-count="">Rate this recipe</h2><div class="vc-form" data-table="feed_data" data-id="1576186" data-rate-hint1="Not good" data-rate-hint2="so so" data-rate-hint3="Good" data-rate-hint4="Very good" data-rate-hint5="Excellent !!!">
