				<section id="rd-qa"><h2 id="ref-qa" class="title">Questions</h2><div id="rd-qa-list"><button type="button" class="btn btn-main btn-block open-modal mb-3" data-action="question"><i class="fal fa-plus fa-fw"></i> Ask a question to the author</button><div class="item"><h3 class="i-title"><i class="fal fa-circle-question fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i> Could I sub sugar for maple syrup or honey?</h3><p class="i-answer">Yes, you can substitute sugar with maple syrup or honey. Use about 3/4 the amount of syrup or honey compared to sugar, and reduce other liquids slightly to keep the batter balanced. It will add a lovely natural sweetness and moisture!</p></div></div></section>				
